# 500 /bin/true spawns per interval, observed at 50/200/1000 ms.
# Ground truth = the (pid,starttime) key read by the launcher itself, so
# the denominator is exact and is not itself a sample.
# Spawns are jittered: without jitter a spawn period that divides the
# poll interval phase-locks and the loss figure becomes an aliasing
# artifact (observed: exactly 0/25/50/100% rather than a curve).
# A window equal to the interval is used so the scan cost (2-4 ms) does
# not itself consume a large fraction of the sampling opportunity.
